  "name": "Question 54",
  "problem": "| $y$ | $1$ | $4$ | $9$ | $16$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(Y=y)$ | $0.4$ | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.1$ |\n\nCompute $P(Y<10)$ given that the random variable $Y$ has the probability mass function shown in the table above.",
  "result": "Correct",
  "worked_solution": "Using the values in the table, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Y<10) & =P(y\\in {1,4,9}) \\\\  & =P(Y=1)+P(Y=4)+P(Y=9) \\\\  & =0.4+0.2+0.3 \\\\  & =0.9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"
